29
00:01:52,470 --> 00:02:00,000
And before we edit the script, let's shed some light on another key programming principle compartmentalization.

30
00:02:00,030 --> 00:02:03,120
Yes, I know it sounds like a big word, but it's an important one.

31
00:02:03,120 --> 00:02:08,490
So let's try to understand what this means with a real world visualization.

32
00:02:08,640 --> 00:02:12,570
Imagine your game as a large, bustling, busy city.

33
00:02:12,600 --> 00:02:16,950
Now, in a city, you wouldn't just jumble up the homes and the offices and the industries and the parks

34
00:02:16,950 --> 00:02:18,240
all in one space, would you?

35
00:02:18,510 --> 00:02:21,900
Instead, you would zone them into districts or compartments.

36
00:02:21,900 --> 00:02:25,950
You'd have residential zones and industrial zones and business zones and parks, etc...

37
00:02:26,280 --> 00:02:30,030
This is the essence of compartmentalization and coding.

38
00:02:30,030 --> 00:02:36,930
By segmenting our code into distinct sections or compartments, each dedicated to a specific function

39
00:02:36,930 --> 00:02:37,710
or task.

40
00:02:37,710 --> 00:02:40,980
And by doing this, we achieve two major benefits.

41
00:02:41,010 --> 00:02:46,680
First, our code becomes much more organized and manageable, just as city officials would only need

42
00:02:46,680 --> 00:02:52,200
to review and manage a specific district for any changes, developers can focus on individual compartments

43
00:02:52,200 --> 00:02:55,710
of code without getting all overwhelmed by the entirety of the code.

44
00:02:55,710 --> 00:03:01,620
And secondly, this approach greatly helps in creating reusable code.

45
00:03:01,650 --> 00:03:06,750
Now, when code sections are compartmentalized effectively, they can often be picked up and placed

46
00:03:06,750 --> 00:03:07,800
into another project.

47
00:03:08,340 --> 00:03:10,380
But maybe just some minimal adjustments.

48
00:03:10,380 --> 00:03:14,490
Just like we reused the obstacle code from our traffic racer game.

